                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9259b95b-fd3b-3758-b7a6-9d7104b50a67",
                        "entry_id": "d9be5d69-6abe-38eb-a65a-3747c4ecaed9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To meet (something) in response to a thing; to counter."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "810ac8e6-bc55-4980-9de9-4e5fb02e0a1f",
                                "sense_id": "9259b95b-fd3b-3758-b7a6-9d7104b50a67",
                                "text": "I admire the question by which you have countermet and rebuked my own."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6075553e-985a-4579-a4f8-8ef3e5f6e649",
                                "sense_id": "9259b95b-fd3b-3758-b7a6-9d7104b50a67",
                                "text": "Yes; and rent, and payments, clothing, food ; how much to plant of this or that, and where; how preserve the soil fertility, check erosion by the sudden rains, rotate the crops to best advantage, countermeet this loss or that."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "43192061-2271-4c94-96d4-8a32508b1552",
                                "sense_id": "9259b95b-fd3b-3758-b7a6-9d7104b50a67",
                                "text": "From the point of view of the Cola ruler , this alliance must have been to coordinate action to countermeet the rivalry offered by the rulers of Bengal and the Sailendras of Sumatra."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c9f6c84b-2617-45d8-8e58-2e07abc35f18",
                                "sense_id": "9259b95b-fd3b-3758-b7a6-9d7104b50a67",
                                "text": "Yet, this desire for invisibility and faithfulness, no doubt here born out of love and awe for the work being translated, of being prudent rather than bold, is countermet by the fact that as translation and creative writing share the same processual nature, that translation is both a creative and critical practice, that the creative text depends on translation for its survival, translators then must share the same responsibility of the writer toward their text, because this is, after all, the verbal embodiment of their own unique reading and response."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
